{
  "benchmark_name": "phase6_grounded_generation_benchmark",
  "benchmark_version": "1.0.0",
  "created": "2026-09-27",
  "purpose": "Phase 6 structural-grounding correctness benchmark: tests whether generation/pipeline.py transforms (ResearchQuery, Evidence[]) into a structurally-grounded GroundedAnswer whose claims/citations satisfy independently-authored gold expectations. NOT a Phase-7 semantic-faithfulness benchmark.",
  "methodology_notes": [
    "Evidence objects were built via evidence/adapters.py from REAL raw records already captured in artifacts/v2/phase5_benchmark_manifest.json's development/validation splits (real NCBI/ClinicalTrials.gov/EBI ChEMBL API responses and real local RAG retrieve() output, fetched during Phase-5 benchmark construction) - no synthetic/fabricated Evidence content anywhere in this benchmark.",
    "Gold expectations (required_fact_substrings, forbidden_substrings, expected_abstain, expect_conflict, min_factual_claims, required_source_types) were authored independently by inspecting each real Evidence object's actual content BEFORE running any candidate - never copied from a candidate's output.",
    "Scale is deliberately smaller than Phase 5's 72-case benchmark (16 total cases) - this is a first Phase-6 benchmark, not a claim of equivalent statistical power; see docs/v2/PHASE6_GROUNDED_GENERATION.md for the explicit scope caveat.",
    "The phase6_heldout split (3 cases) reuses the same underlying real Evidence pool as development/validation (same brigatinib/imatinib/melanoma real records) under fresh query framings and independently-authored gold never inspected before the single held-out run - consistent with the Phase 4/5 precedent of reusing real source material across splits while keeping gold labels and scoring genuinely untouched until freeze.",
    "One held-out case (P6-H2) asked about a ChEMBL 'alogp' value that does not exist in the frozen Phase-5 ChemblEvidenceMetadata schema (only molecule_type/max_phase/mechanism_of_action/match_type are captured) - this was a gold-authoring error discovered via the held-out run, not a generation-system defect; see docs/v2/PHASE6_GATE_PLAN.md failure analysis and PHASE6_FINAL_GATE_AUDIT.md for the full accounting. The held-out split is SPENT and was not rerun."
  ],
  "split_sizes": {
    "development": 10,
    "validation": 3,
    "phase6_heldout": 3
  },
